mode: "100644"
text: "# Formats, fit, safety + two worked examples\n\n## Format + platform literacy (verify-quarterly)\n| Platform | Meme shape | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| TikTok | video + trending sound, green screen, duet | best distribution; trending audio = licensing risk for brands (ai-music-and-sound) |\n| X | reactive screenshot + pithy text; copypasta | wit + speed; real-time conversation |\n| LinkedIn | work-life / industry humor | witty not edgy; 1-2/week mixed with substance |\n| Reddit | meme-native, subreddit-specific | participate genuinely -- brand broadcasting gets downvoted |\n| Instagram | image macro + Reels | volume; carousel + reaction formats |\nFormats: classic image macro (picture + text), reaction image, \"which one are you\", \"tag a friend who...\", nostalgia, self-own/meta, niche in-group joke.\n\n## The brand-fit filter\n```\n[ ] Matches our voice/audience/values (not just \"it's funny\")\n[ ] Would work even WITHOUT our logo on it\n[ ] Niche/specific enough that our in-group says \"I see you\"\n[ ] We genuinely understand it (not faking fluency)\n-> if it fails, sit it out + use an evergreen on-brand format instead\n```\n\n## Safety -- the \"don't\" list\n```\nNO tragedies / disasters / sensitive events    NO divisive politics / culture-war bait\nNO private moments / real people without consent NO appropriation of a culture/subculture that isn't yours\nNO punching down at any group                    RESEARCH the origin + connotations first   (\"if you have to ask, don't\")\n```\n\n## IP checklist\n```\n[ ] Original meme visual (AI + human pass / custom photo / commissioned) -- not a copyrighted character\n[ ] No celebrity/identifiable-person likeness used commercially without permission -- real OR an AI lookalike (2026 likeness crisis: actionable under US state right-of-publicity law; federal NO FAKES Act advancing -- verify-quarterly)\n[ ] Catchphrase not trademarked by its creator\n[ ] Trending audio cleared/licensed for a brand (or skip it) -> ai-music-and-sound\n[ ] Credit the original creator when remixing UGC\n```\n\n## Execution playbook\n```\nLo-fi + authentic > high-budget. Self-aware/self-deprecating/meta humor. AI for concepts -> HUMAN adds the final\n~10% wit + sensitivity screen (beat the AI-slop filter). Cut approvals to ~1 person -> react in hours. Keep 40-50% of\nthe calendar open for reactive posts. Measure dark-social shares + brand search, not just likes.\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 - B2B SaaS, niche meme (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nOur audience: ops managers. The meme: a hyper-specific \"the report that could've been a dashboard\" format -- works without\nour logo, lands only if you live that pain. Original visual in ideogram (no copyrighted character). One-person approval, posted\nsame day on LinkedIn + X. No tragedy, no trending-audio risk. If a format doesn't fit ops humor, I skip it -- forced is worse than nothing.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 - cafe brand, cultural moment (warm studio voice)\n```\nA gentle, on-brand take on a seasonal moment our regulars actually share -- nothing divisive, nothing borrowed from a culture\nthat isn't ours. We build an original graphic in our template (design-and-templates), keep it warm and self-aware, and add the\nhuman touch that makes it feel like us. If the trend doesn't suit our voice, we let it pass and post something evergreen instead -- one small, safe step.\n```\n\nBoth: format understood + on-brand + safe + original visual; lo-fi + human-finished; posted fast or sat out; never a\ncopyrighted character, a tragedy, or a borrowed culture; relevance never faked.\n"
